  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased Demand and Engagement for Accountability (IDEA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Sri Lanka):  |Civil society advocacy plays an important role in advancing good governance reforms, as seen clearly in Sri Lanka in 2022. Through the Increased Demand and Engagement for Accountability (IDEA) activity, USAID supports an improved enabling environment for civil society, and strengthens the organizational capacity and sustainability of civil society organizations (CSOs).With FY 2022 resources, USAID will fully obligate the mortgage of IDEA activity.  With FY 22 resources, USAID will continue to provide post-award administration, management, and capacity building for three sister USAID awards to local Sri Lankan CSOs. This activity will also conduct an organizational capacity assessment to develop a capacity building program for participating CSOs to meet standardized USAID mission requirements and build their capacity to directly manage USAID funds after IDEA ends.FY2022 resources will also strengthen the enabling environment for civil society in Sri Lanka and will prepare scenarios to safeguard CSO operational space and prevent backsliding.Through this activity, USAID advances the US Embassy Integrated Country Strategy Mission Objective 2.3: &apos;Bolster civil society and free and independent media&apos; and the Country Development Cooperation Strategy Development Objective 1: &apos;Effective Democratic Governance Strengthened&apos;.$847,000 within this IM will contribute to the required DRG directive of $15,100,000, and $50,000 within this IM contributes to the TIP earmark of $350,000.. .. ... .</narrative>
  </description>
